[2026-01-30T16:58:10.984Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_014NjNRAzXZXJ3gPSPzSEGeg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Shell Protocol Implementation Complete\n\nI've created a composable shell/layout protocol system that allows content to declare its shell requirements and compose them declaratively. Here's a summary:\n\n### Created: `src/lib/shell/`\n\n| File | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `protocol.ts` | Core types, defaults, and resolution utilities |\n| `context.tsx` | ShellProvider and useShell hook for content |\n| `containers.tsx` | Container implementations (Modal, Drawer, Panel, etc.) |\n| `index.ts` | Module exports |\n\n### Key Types & Interfaces\n\n**ShellRequirements** - What content declares:\n- `backdrop` - Blur, opacity, close on click\n- `animation` - Preset ('scale', 'slide', 'fade') or custom motion props\n- `keyboard` - Escape to close, focus trap, custom handlers\n- `scroll` - Body lock, restore position\n- `size` - Width/height presets or CSS values\n- `theme` - Border radius, shadow, border style\n\n**ShellContext** - What container provides:\n- `containerType` - modal, drawer, panel, page, inline\n- `isOpen`, `close` - State and action\n- `registerKeyHandler` - Dynamic keyboard bindings\n- `updateRequirements` - Content can update requirements dynamically\n\n### Container Components\n\n| Container | Features |\n|-----------|----------|\n| `ModalContainer` | Centered overlay, backdrop, focus trap |\n| `DrawerContainer` | Slide from edge (left/right/top/bottom) |\n| `PanelContainer` | Inline panel, no overlay |\n| `ReportShellContainer` | Full-viewport with ambient effects |\n| `ShellContainer` | Universal wrapper, picks container by type |\n\n### Updated: `src/components/report/ReportShell.tsx`\n- Now uses `useShell` hook to declare its requirements\n- Exports `REPORT_SHELL_REQUIREMENTS` for reuse\n- Same visual appearance, but now protocol-aware\n\n### Benefits\n- **Same content, different containers**: A view can render in modal, drawer, or page context without code changes\n- **Declarative composition**: Content declares what it needs, containers provide it\n- **Dynamic updates**: Content can update requirements at runtime\n- **Consistent behavior**: Keyboard, focus, scroll handling centralized\n- **Theme-aware**: Swiss and radar themes supported"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":307,"cache_read_input_tokens":133043,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":307},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb700aba-f9fc-4283-93cf-561e37220b63","uuid":"7a04e8fa-05fc-46f8-82b6-139cfa038212"}
